00:42:05.670 --> 00:42:07.070
Oh, Maxine Fortenberry.

1037
00:42:07.270 --> 00:42:08.230
I love True Blood.

1038
00:42:08.430 --> 00:42:09.410
She was fantastic.

1039
00:42:09.730 --> 00:42:11.010
Of course, you would know that.

1040
00:42:11.130 --> 00:42:11.410
Yes.

1041
00:42:11.610 --> 00:42:13.570
I have a crossover connection with Dale.

1042
00:42:13.830 --> 00:42:14.290
Tell me.

1043
00:42:14.450 --> 00:42:16.590
We were both on Fresh Off the Boat.

1044
00:42:16.990 --> 00:42:17.710
Well, there you go.

1045
00:42:17.850 --> 00:42:21.210
Not Monk, surprisingly, but Fresh Off the Boat.

1046
00:42:21.210 --> 00:42:23.150
Well, she will come back in season six.

1047
00:42:23.430 --> 00:42:25.790
This is not the last we're going to see of Ronnie.

1048
00:42:26.430 --> 00:42:29.910
Meanwhile, we're going to see Pam in her first class.

1049
00:42:30.170 --> 00:42:31.370
She looks so cute.

1050
00:42:31.670 --> 00:42:34.010
She has, like, I'm calling it the college ponytail.

1051
00:42:34.290 --> 00:42:36.770
She wears this really cute ponytail at school.

1052
00:42:37.110 --> 00:42:37.470
All right.

1053
00:42:37.570 --> 00:42:40.390
The ponytail is the only thing that's cute about Pam.

1054
00:42:40.650 --> 00:42:41.310
Are you kidding?

1055
00:42:41.330 --> 00:42:44.010
I thought you looked so cute in all of your college scenes.

1056
00:42:44.290 --> 00:42:47.570
Did you notice how young everyone else is in the class?

1057
00:42:47.590 --> 00:42:48.750
Oh, you stop it.

1058
00:42:48.750 --> 00:42:50.570
No, but this was a deliberate choice.

1059
00:42:50.850 --> 00:42:51.410
Well, okay.

1060
00:42:51.830 --> 00:42:53.470
Pam is in her late 20s.

1061
00:42:53.470 --> 00:42:56.110
Do you like how immediately I, like, stand up for my best friend?

1062
00:42:56.110 --> 00:42:57.210
I'm like, you stop it.

1063
00:42:57.270 --> 00:42:58.170
You are beautiful.

1064
00:42:58.530 --> 00:43:00.850
You look just as young as those other ones.

1065
00:43:01.150 --> 00:43:01.200
That's right.

1066
00:43:01.270 --> 00:43:02.450
And you are smart.

1067
00:43:03.030 --> 00:43:03.310
Okay.

1068
00:43:03.310 --> 00:43:03.790
Thank you.

1069
00:43:03.930 --> 00:43:04.310
You're welcome.

1070
00:43:04.590 --> 00:43:07.270
I want you to know I was not being down on myself.

1071
00:43:07.270 --> 00:43:10.690
I was just pointing out a deliberate production choice.

1072
00:43:11.290 --> 00:43:15.610
Pam is in her late 20s, and they made sure that everyone in this class,

1073
00:43:15.770 --> 00:43:17.990
that the background performers were all much younger.

1074
00:43:17.990 --> 00:43:20.050
They're just starting off in college, right?

1075
00:43:20.250 --> 00:43:21.530
Pam's going back to school.

1076
00:43:21.650 --> 00:43:26.870
And they did want to create this story for Pam that she is kind of, you know.

1077
00:43:27.870 --> 00:43:28.350
Yeah.

1078
00:43:28.590 --> 00:43:29.050
I don't know.

1079
00:43:29.050 --> 00:43:29.670
What am I saying?

1080
00:43:29.690 --> 00:43:30.270
What do they call it?

1081
00:43:30.310 --> 00:43:31.450
A non-traditional student.

1082
00:43:31.690 --> 00:43:32.250
There you go.

1083
00:43:32.670 --> 00:43:35.250
Well, not only that, she's in the wrong class.

1084
00:43:35.810 --> 00:43:40.590
The teacher, who was played by Sandra Lowe, Professor Monaghan.

1085
00:43:40.590 --> 00:43:47.670
She's got that zinger of a joke about Zaf Chancery, you know, which, by the way, I read

1086
00:43:47.670 --> 00:43:50.430
a Reddit thread where people were like, that doesn't apply.

1087
00:43:50.850 --> 00:43:51.770
It's wrong.

1088
00:43:52.190 --> 00:43:52.550
Oh.

1089
00:43:53.190 --> 00:43:53.950
Oh, my.

1090
00:43:54.130 --> 00:43:56.350
Well, Pam does not end up leaving the class.

1091
00:43:56.470 --> 00:43:57.270
And we got some mail.

1092
00:43:57.410 --> 00:44:00.470
People were like, Pam has been so good about standing up for herself.

1093
00:44:00.890 --> 00:44:02.570
Why doesn't she just leave the class?

1094
00:44:02.770 --> 00:44:03.430
I don't know.

1095
00:44:03.430 --> 00:44:04.550
I sympathized.

1096
00:44:04.670 --> 00:44:06.010
I felt like she's new here.

1097
00:44:06.010 --> 00:44:07.070
She feels out of place.

1098
00:44:07.250 --> 00:44:08.710
She just got singled out.

1099
00:44:08.850 --> 00:44:12.750
She's going to tuck her head down and know she'll do it right the next time.

1100
00:44:12.990 --> 00:44:13.230
Yeah.

1101
00:44:13.450 --> 00:44:17.770
But I guess it's going to mean she misses her actual first real class.

1102
00:44:19.450 --> 00:44:23.430
Back in the office, Holly hears this coughing, right?

1103
00:44:23.610 --> 00:44:24.890
She's at her cubicle.

1104
00:44:25.350 --> 00:44:26.270
Kelly is coughing.

1105
00:44:26.550 --> 00:44:27.630
She sounds sick.

1106
00:44:28.110 --> 00:44:31.230
Did you notice on Holly's desk what her nameplate says?

1107
00:44:31.510 --> 00:44:32.030
Yes.

1108
00:44:32.850 --> 00:44:33.370
Hollis.

1109
00:44:33.870 --> 00:44:36.410
And then in quotes, Holly P.

1110
00:44:37.150 --> 00:44:37.590
Flax.

1111
00:44:38.230 --> 00:44:39.350
I did notice that.

1112
00:44:39.350 --> 00:44:40.330
So that's her real name.

1113
00:44:40.490 --> 00:44:41.250
Her name is Hollis.

1114
00:44:41.530 --> 00:44:41.970
Hollis.

1115
00:44:42.490 --> 00:44:47.690
Kelly has a talking head where she says she's on the third day of her cleanse diet where she's

1116
00:44:47.690 --> 00:44:51.070
doing the lemon juice, maple syrup, and cayenne pepper and water.

1117
00:44:51.350 --> 00:44:53.090
That's all she's allowed to have.

1118
00:44:53.710 --> 00:44:55.670
Angela, have you ever done any of these fad diets?

1119
00:44:56.050 --> 00:45:00.170
I haven't, but I had a roommate who did something with cayenne pepper and water.

1120
00:45:00.370 --> 00:45:02.710
And I think it just gives you the runs, right?

1121
00:45:02.710 --> 00:45:03.510
You just poop.

1122
00:45:03.770 --> 00:45:09.510
You know, I got approached to do an ad for this diet tea that's supposed to flatten your tummy.

1123
00:45:09.790 --> 00:45:10.930
So you drink the tea.

1124
00:45:11.130 --> 00:45:12.530
And it flattens your tummy.

1125
00:45:12.730 --> 00:45:13.090
How?

1126
00:45:13.390 --> 00:45:15.590
By making you poop a lot.

1127
00:45:15.770 --> 00:45:15.950
Well.

1128
00:45:16.290 --> 00:45:18.270
But it was like a cleansing tea.

1129
00:45:18.810 --> 00:45:23.470
And I was like, well, first of all, I'm not going to do an ad for anything I don't believe in.

1130
00:45:23.470 --> 00:45:23.870
Mm-hmm.

1131
00:45:24.130 --> 00:45:26.870
So send me the tea and we'll see what happens.

1132
00:45:27.190 --> 00:45:28.410
Did you drink the tea?

1133
00:45:28.590 --> 00:45:32.550
I was doing splitting up together at the time and I was talking to Oliver Hudson about it.

1134
00:45:32.610 --> 00:45:33.850
And he said, I'll do it with you.

1135
00:45:33.930 --> 00:45:36.670
Let's both do the tea and see if we get flat tummies.

1136
00:45:37.050 --> 00:45:37.970
He's so funny.

1137
00:45:37.970 --> 00:45:41.790
But I can so hear him saying that because he's just like, let's do it.

1138
00:45:41.850 --> 00:45:42.690
He was all in.

1139
00:45:42.690 --> 00:45:44.990
So I asked for two packages of the tea.

1140
00:45:45.570 --> 00:45:47.290
Oliver and I started doing it.

1141
00:45:47.410 --> 00:45:47.730
Angela.

1142
00:45:47.990 --> 00:45:48.810
Did you poop?

1143
00:45:49.210 --> 00:45:51.130
First of all, I gained weight.

1144
00:45:51.370 --> 00:45:51.850
What?

1145
00:45:52.350 --> 00:45:55.570
Second of all, we're just pooping and farting.

1146
00:45:55.570 --> 00:45:56.050
Oh, no.

1147
00:45:56.490 --> 00:45:58.950
We're trying to work and do our scenes.

1148
00:45:59.230 --> 00:45:59.450
Oh, no.

1149
00:45:59.450 --> 00:46:02.210
The crew was like, stop drinking the tea, you guys.

1150
00:46:02.330 --> 00:46:03.810
You're like, we're farting them out.

1151
00:46:03.970 --> 00:46:09.290
They're like, seriously, we cannot have the two leads of our show drinking this tea.

1152
00:46:09.470 --> 00:46:11.310
Being so flatulent on set.

1153
00:46:11.310 --> 00:46:12.810
It's ruining everything.

1154
00:46:13.130 --> 00:46:15.410
So I just, I don't know.

1155
00:46:15.610 --> 00:46:17.290
I just don't do this stuff.

1156
00:46:17.570 --> 00:46:18.630
Well, you know my husband.

1157
00:46:18.630 --> 00:46:19.610
He's super healthy.

1158
00:46:19.750 --> 00:46:23.130
And he just makes really good choices about what he eats.

1159
00:46:23.730 --> 00:46:25.270
And he exercises.

1160
00:46:25.570 --> 00:46:28.470
It's really annoying, his ability to be so consistent.

1161
00:46:28.790 --> 00:46:30.530
My hardest struggle is consistency.

1162
00:46:30.810 --> 00:46:31.170
You know?

1163
00:46:31.350 --> 00:46:33.910
Just like making that space for myself.

1164
00:46:34.170 --> 00:46:38.530
And I think it's even like when you peel back the layer, it's like making that time for yourself.

1165
00:46:38.690 --> 00:46:39.990
And it's just a hard thing to do.

1166
00:46:40.430 --> 00:46:40.750
Yeah.

1167
00:46:41.310 --> 00:46:47.750
Well, I think we should take a break because I need a moment to center myself before Jan comes into the office.

1168
00:46:48.290 --> 00:46:49.430
Oh, oh, yes.

1169
00:46:49.530 --> 00:46:52.190
And there's some really good Jan stuff I want to share.

1170
00:46:52.670 --> 00:46:53.150
All right.

1171
00:46:53.210 --> 00:46:53.950
We'll be right back.

1172
00:47:04.410 --> 00:47:05.530
We are back.

1173
00:47:05.810 --> 00:47:07.030
And so is Jan.

1174
00:47:07.370 --> 00:47:07.790
Oh, yeah.

1175
00:47:08.310 --> 00:47:13.130
Jan enters the office and tells Ronnie to make her some copies of a document on canary yellow paper.

1176
00:47:13.350 --> 00:47:13.710
Oh, yeah.

1177
00:47:13.750 --> 00:47:15.190
She walks in like she owns the place.

1178
00:47:15.330 --> 00:47:18.750
She also does not acknowledge that she's speaking to a person she's never met.

1179
00:47:18.930 --> 00:47:19.410
Oh, yeah.

1180
00:47:19.410 --> 00:47:19.910
Yeah, that's true.

1181
00:47:20.310 --> 00:47:27.470
This made me wonder if Jan is entertaining Michael being in her life again so she can just use him and use the office.

1182
00:47:27.610 --> 00:47:29.130
She's getting free copies, right?

1183
00:47:29.330 --> 00:47:29.530
Yeah.

1184
00:47:29.530 --> 00:47:33.410
Well, in the deleted scenes, there's a little bit of a runner about this.

1185
00:47:33.610 --> 00:47:37.270
She is giving Michael like a list of things she needs him to do.

1186
00:47:37.450 --> 00:47:38.610
All her errands.

1187
00:47:38.710 --> 00:47:39.530
Go to the dry cleaner.

1188
00:47:39.690 --> 00:47:40.770
She hands him a bag.

1189
00:47:40.970 --> 00:47:42.670
Like grocery shopping, etc.

1190
00:47:42.670 --> 00:47:44.990
Like Michael is her personal assistant.

1191
00:47:45.650 --> 00:47:50.290
And then when he kind of boxed at anything, she's like, well, I thought you wanted to help.

1192
00:47:50.570 --> 00:47:51.010
Wow.

1193
00:47:51.010 --> 00:47:53.290
So, to me, I feel like Jan is using him.

1194
00:47:53.470 --> 00:47:53.990
For sure.

1195
00:47:54.490 --> 00:48:02.930
Jim has this talking head where he says, Michael led us to believe he was the father of Jan's baby by telling us he was the father of Jan's baby.

1196
00:48:03.230 --> 00:48:05.310
Well, this talking head would have continued.

1197
00:48:05.570 --> 00:48:05.990
Oh.

1198
00:48:05.990 --> 00:48:06.970
And they had to trim it.

1199
00:48:06.970 --> 00:48:13.050
And Jim then holds up an email and says, but then Jan sent this email to everyone.

1200
00:48:13.210 --> 00:48:15.070
And here's what Jan's email said.

1201
00:48:15.310 --> 00:48:16.190
Hi, everyone.

1202
00:48:16.350 --> 00:48:20.350
Jan here writing to share some wonderful news and to squash a rumor.

1203
00:48:20.790 --> 00:48:23.350
First, the great news I am expecting.

1204
00:48:23.770 --> 00:48:33.010
The beautiful baby girl inside me will be ready to meet the world this fall, just a few months before the launch of the new Serenity by Jan line.

1205
00:48:33.350 --> 00:48:34.610
Shameless plug, I know.

1206
00:48:34.750 --> 00:48:35.310
Don't hate me.

1207
00:48:35.430 --> 00:48:35.690
LOL.

1208
00:48:35.690 --> 00:48:44.890
Well, anyway, I also wanted to clarify that the father is not anyone that you or I have ever met.

1209
00:48:45.330 --> 00:48:53.030
Remember, no matter how excited someone is about my baby, it does not make them the father.

1210
00:48:53.630 --> 00:48:54.730
Best Jan.

1211
00:48:54.990 --> 00:48:55.410
P.S.

1212
00:48:55.490 --> 00:48:57.230
Hope to ship you something soon.

1213
00:48:57.690 --> 00:48:58.610
That's amazing.

1214
00:48:58.810 --> 00:48:58.970
Yeah.

1215
00:48:59.290 --> 00:49:01.850
So, she sent that email to everyone in the office.

1216
00:49:02.110 --> 00:49:04.650
Well, Holly would like to know who is Jan.

1217
00:49:04.650 --> 00:49:07.770
She says, who's that woman in Michael's office with the feet?

1218
00:49:08.010 --> 00:49:10.270
Because Michael is rubbing Jan's feet.

1219
00:49:10.830 --> 00:49:14.990
Oscar explains that she's Michael's ex-girlfriend.

1220
00:49:15.550 --> 00:49:21.190
And Holly immediately decides, yes, you can give your yoga teacher my number.

1221
00:49:21.350 --> 00:49:23.310
I want to date your hot yoga teacher.

1222
00:49:23.470 --> 00:49:23.790
Yeah.

1223
00:49:24.370 --> 00:49:26.090
His hot, hot yoga teacher.

1224
00:49:26.090 --> 00:49:28.510
Because he teaches hot yoga and he's hot.

1225
00:49:28.510 --> 00:49:30.650
So, I'm sure he's very bendy.

1226
00:49:31.110 --> 00:49:31.510
Yeah.

1227
00:49:31.830 --> 00:49:32.050
Yeah.

1228
00:49:32.850 --> 00:49:37.630
Then, Holly overhears Angela berating Kevin for being an idiot.

1229
00:49:37.990 --> 00:49:40.130
And Holly is going to come to Kevin's defense.

1230
00:49:40.270 --> 00:49:45.570
Because remember, Dwight told Holly that Kevin was there as part of a special work program.

1231
00:49:45.730 --> 00:49:45.930
Yeah.

1232
00:49:46.010 --> 00:49:47.270
When Dwight was hazing her.

1233
00:49:47.570 --> 00:49:47.790
Yeah.

1234
00:49:47.790 --> 00:49:51.490
Oh, she runs over to Angela and she's like, how dare you?

1235
00:49:51.610 --> 00:49:53.310
You don't speak to him like that.

1236
00:49:53.530 --> 00:49:58.370
And this is when everyone realizes, including Kevin, what Dwight told Holly.

1237
00:49:58.790 --> 00:50:01.190
Angela is so delighted by this moment.

1238
00:50:01.450 --> 00:50:01.810
Mm-hmm.

1239
00:50:01.990 --> 00:50:03.250
She can't stop smiling.

1240
00:50:03.630 --> 00:50:06.690
No, she loves that Holly has been humiliated.

1241
00:50:06.870 --> 00:50:07.130
Mm-hmm.

1242
00:50:07.430 --> 00:50:07.990
Poor Kevin.

1243
00:50:08.190 --> 00:50:09.010
He's crushed.

1244
00:50:09.210 --> 00:50:13.430
This means that Holly has not been paying attention to him because she wants to date him.

1245
00:50:13.550 --> 00:50:13.870
No.

1246
00:50:14.050 --> 00:50:14.870
He's realizing.

1247
00:50:14.870 --> 00:50:18.270
Well, now Andy is going to approach Angela in the kitchen.

1248
00:50:18.270 --> 00:50:24.090
He has made non-refundable deposits at four different wedding locations.

1249
00:50:24.430 --> 00:50:26.350
Hot air balloons over Napa Valley.

1250
00:50:26.550 --> 00:50:26.870
Mm-hmm.

1251
00:50:27.030 --> 00:50:29.430
World-famous Walt Disney's Epcot Center.

1252
00:50:29.710 --> 00:50:30.050
Mm-hmm.

1253
00:50:30.190 --> 00:50:32.230
Scuba diving wedding in the Bahamas.

1254
00:50:32.710 --> 00:50:35.110
And the Wilkes Bar Marriott Ballroom C.

1255
00:50:35.510 --> 00:50:40.830
To which she replies, dangerous, tacky, sharks, haunted.

1256
00:50:41.430 --> 00:50:42.430
And no.

1257
00:50:42.890 --> 00:50:43.510
And, oh.

1258
00:50:43.510 --> 00:50:44.190
Just in general.

1259
00:50:44.770 --> 00:50:45.790
And no.

1260
00:50:46.930 --> 00:50:51.450
And, of course, this means Angela and Dwight are going to hook up again.

1261
00:50:51.690 --> 00:50:53.150
We had a fan question.

1262
00:50:53.470 --> 00:50:53.770
Mm-hmm.

1263
00:50:54.070 --> 00:51:00.350
Kayla would like to know, when Dwight slaps Angela's butt, was that scripted because she

1264
00:51:00.350 --> 00:51:02.070
thought your reaction was very genuine?

1265
00:51:02.090 --> 00:51:03.250
You were surprised.

1266
00:51:03.530 --> 00:51:04.970
No, that was improvised.

1267
00:51:05.210 --> 00:51:05.610
Mm-hmm.

1268
00:51:05.730 --> 00:51:06.650
That was Rainn Wilson.

1269
00:51:06.650 --> 00:51:08.230
But now, listen, you guys.

1270
00:51:08.470 --> 00:51:10.490
Rainn and I were very, very good friends.

1271
00:51:10.790 --> 00:51:14.510
And we would always do a few takes where we would try to surprise each other a little

1272
00:51:14.510 --> 00:51:18.390
bit within the boundaries of what I knew would not make anyone uncomfortable and vice versa.

1273
00:51:18.690 --> 00:51:18.830
Right.

1274
00:51:18.830 --> 00:51:24.450
And so, no, that was Rainn, just mixing it up and catching me off guard, which is why my

1275
00:51:24.450 --> 00:51:25.790
reaction is so earneSt.

1276
00:51:25.790 --> 00:51:31.810
We also got mail from Alice, who would like to ask, Angela, in your talking head afterwards,

1277
00:51:32.290 --> 00:51:33.850
was any of that improvised?

1278
00:51:33.930 --> 00:51:35.670
Because it's one of my all-time favorites.

1279
00:51:35.670 --> 00:51:36.610
You know what?

1280
00:51:36.850 --> 00:51:40.690
People quote this talking head to me, and it was completely scripted.

1281
00:51:40.830 --> 00:51:45.250
And it read like this, I have a nice comforter and several cozy pillows.

1282
00:51:45.590 --> 00:51:49.330
I usually read a chapter of a book, and it's lights out by 8.30.

1283
00:51:49.890 --> 00:51:51.490
That's how I sleep at night.

1284
00:51:52.450 --> 00:51:53.410
Completely scripted.

1285
00:51:54.250 --> 00:51:55.690
You go to bed at 8.30.

1286
00:51:55.890 --> 00:51:56.350
I know.

1287
00:51:56.750 --> 00:51:58.610
I have lots of cats to take care of.

1288
00:51:58.670 --> 00:51:59.310
They get up early.

1289
